(493615, 47326, 7628, '<td valign="top">Hi, I looked at your forum thread, and as you requested i''m responding here.  I reallly like this idea, and while the lighting must have been tough, you did a good job. Still wish the focus on the hand and can had been sharper, or perhaps some light from the side to throw more shadows on the hand and show more texture in the flesh and more dimensionality.  I like your white glove idea, but that would have been hard to light too.  I like the simplicity, and sterile feeling a glove would add ( maybe even a plastic glove?)  The whole image is a bit busy - there are all those holograms on the disk which lean my eye away from the bug spray, which is where the real joke is.  How about using the other side of the disc?  the move the hand and can more into the frame - I stil think you should include mor of the thumb. And if we could see a bit more of the can it would make it more central focus, then the eye would go to the disc, and, "a ha!" they''d get the joke.  I say give your white glove idea a try, I''d love to see the results.</td>', 'Hi, I looked at your forum thread, and as you requested i''m responding here.  I reallly like this idea, and while the lighting must have been tough, you did a good job. Still wish the focus on the hand and can had been sharper, or perhaps some light from the side to throw more shadows on the hand and show more texture in the flesh and more dimensionality.  I like your white glove idea, but that would have been hard to light too.  I like the simplicity, and sterile feeling a glove would add ( maybe even a plastic glove?)  The whole image is a bit busy - there are all those holograms on the disk which lean my eye away from the bug spray, which is where the real joke is.  How about using the other side of the disc?  the move the hand and can more into the frame - I stil think you should include mor of the thumb. And if we could see a bit more of the can it would make it more central focus, then the eye would go to the disc, and, "a ha!" they''d get the joke.  I say give your white glove idea a try, I''d love to see the results.', '2003-11-24 13:59:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(493620, 47326, 7628, '<td valign="top">I forgot - how would it work in b&amp;w?  Esp with the other side of the disc up could provide nice texture/brightness contrast with the can and hand.</td>', 'I forgot - how would it work in b&w?  Esp with the other side of the disc up could provide nice texture/brightness contrast with the can and hand.', '2003-11-24 14:02:39.000000', NULL, 0),
